* Title
#+begin_answer
Adaptive Video Streaming Bitrate Selection
#+end_answer

* Abstract
#+begin_answer
Adaptive video streaming is where you maximize the user's Quality of Experience (QoE) by delivering the highest possible video quality while minimizing buffering, playback interruptions, and frequent quality switches.

The agent over here is the video streaming client that decides which bitrate to request for the next video segment.

- Higher bitrate would mean positive reward
- Buffering would mean large negative reward
- Frequent bitrate changes would mean penalty
#+end_answer
